cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datalib: survey microdata as a versioned asset"
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for building and querying an IHSN-organized archive of survey
  microdata, in Stata, R and Python. It treats a survey vintage as a versioned
  asset with a stable identifier, so an analysis can name the exact data it ran
  on. In production at the World Bank and at UNICEF, and published as a worked
  example for any institution standing up an archive of its own.
type: software
